Iris-3B-Metal
Copyright 2026 the Iris-3B-Metal authors

An Apple Silicon inference engine built on the Iris-3B repository
(https://github.com/speridlabs/iris-3b, revision a8d1523). It is not an
official Speridlabs release.

Added: src/iris_metal/, apps/macos/, benchmarks/, assets/metal/,
assets/downstream/, assets/benchmarks/, scripts/benchmark.py, scripts/compare_runs.py,
scripts/denoise_fixture.py, scripts/evaluate.py, scripts/plot_benchmarks.py,
scripts/precision_study.py, scripts/restore_study.py, tests/test_metal_*.py,
tests/test_compare_runs.py, tests/test_data_retries.py, .github/, and the
CHANGELOG, CONTRIBUTING and SECURITY documents.
Modified upstream files: README.md (now about this engine; the upstream README
is kept unchanged as UPSTREAM_README.md), pyproject.toml (package name,
inference-only default dependencies, a "train" extra for the upstream training
stack, the iris-metal command), and .gitignore. Upstream Python sources,
scripts and tests use consistent formatting; src/iris3b/data/datasets.py
also keeps corrupt-sample retries within the batch's shape bucket.
src/iris3b/sampling.py includes the official deterministic Turbo sampler from
Speridlabs revision cee0c130a62a9c288ad8918f1f7cdf23cc228d69.
Inference-only changes that keep results bit-identical: src/iris3b/sampling.py
checks the final Turbo sample before clamping; models/dit.py,
models/blocks/{mmdit,single_stream}.py and
nn/{norms,mlp,embeddings,modulation}.py reuse conditioning and casts, keep
single-stream tokens joined, fuse normalization epilogues on Apple GPUs and
bound per-size caches; flow/solver.py builds guidance inputs once; downstream/restoration.py
skips unused colour-fix work. Training and gradient paths are unchanged.
Turbo validation utilities: scripts/validate_turbo.py,
scripts/pair_turbo_storage.py and scripts/profile_generation.py.

No model weights are included. At runtime the engine downloads the unmodified
Iris-3B Original or Turbo checkpoint (https://huggingface.co/speridlabs/iris-3b) and
Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct), both
under the Apache License 2.0, at the revisions it was validated against.
